OSKit Mouse Driver — Mouse Event Server

Handles mouse IRQ 2. Reads position and button state from the
device and notifies a registered listener thread (typically the
display server). The listener calls mouse_read() to get the
current state.

Device registers (at 0x100090):
- +0 = STATUS (bit 0 = event ready)
- +1 = BUTTONS (reading clears ready flag and lowers IRQ)
- +2 = X_HI, +3 = X_LO (16-bit x position)
- +4 = Y_HI, +5 = Y_LO (16-bit y position)

    module oskit

    val MOUSE_BASE = 0x100090
    val MOUSE_IRQ = 2

    extern register_irq(irq: int, handler: i64)

Current mouse state, updated by the ISR. The display server
reads these directly after being notified.

    var mouse_x = 0
    var mouse_y = 0
    var mouse_buttons = 0
    var mouse_notify_tid = -1

    mouse_set_notify(tid: int)
        mouse_notify_tid = tid

    mouse_init()
        register_irq(MOUSE_IRQ, mouse_handler)

mouse_handler -- Called by the generic IRQ dispatcher.

Reads the device registers and stores current state. Notifies
the registered listener thread so it can update the cursor.

    mouse_handler()
        var status: *i8 = *i8(MOUSE_BASE)
        if (*status & 1) != 0
            var xhi: *i8 = *i8(MOUSE_BASE + 2)
            var xlo: *i8 = *i8(MOUSE_BASE + 3)
            var yhi: *i8 = *i8(MOUSE_BASE + 4)
            var ylo: *i8 = *i8(MOUSE_BASE + 5)
            var btn: *i8 = *i8(MOUSE_BASE + 1)
            mouse_x = ((int(*xhi) & 0xFF) << 8) | (int(*xlo) & 0xFF)
            mouse_y = ((int(*yhi) & 0xFF) << 8) | (int(*ylo) & 0xFF)
            mouse_buttons = int(*btn) & 0xFF
            if mouse_notify_tid >= 0
                notify_send(mouse_notify_tid, 2)
